From 3de49e6f6eb3145a2a3291cf8648bacdea1cfb49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dimitri John Ledkov <dimitri.ledkov@chainguard.dev>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 15:00:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Revert "fips: Align PKCS5_PBKDF2_HMAC defaults with
 EVP_KDF-PBKDF2"

This reverts commit 66ab2db185ac6e473d1a445e20687b9468ba344e.

PKCS5_PBKDF2_HMAC() goes back to always setting the PKCS5 parameter,
which disables the SP 800-132 lower bound checks for both the default
and the FIPS provider, as it did in OpenSSL 3.x.

The CHANGES.md and NEWS.md hunks are not reverted, as they conflict
with later release notes on the 4.0 branch.

test/certs/leaf-encrypted.key is also kept as is: it was only
re-encrypted with a longer salt, which works either way.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
